## Context

« Le système a besoin d'une mémoire dédiée au scraping. Chaque bailleur a ses
pratiques et sa façon de le présenter sur son site » (the author, 2026-09-25)
[the system needs a memory dedicated to scraping; each donor has its own
practices and its own way of presenting them on its site].
As of 2026-09-25: 301 sources on 100 hosts, 64 of them single-source; leading
are portfolio.jetp.id (48), justenergytransition.co.za (34), jetp.moit.gov.vn
(20), aner.sn (15), adb.org (9).

## Actions

1. One file per distributor, `config/jetp-sites/<site>.md`, created **from three
   documents on** or at the first fact worth keeping (blocking, certificate,
   links to follow, living document). YAML header read by the collector: hosts,
   starting collection tier, delay, TLS policy, link patterns to follow,
   recollection class and frequency, witness document, the site's position
   (robots.txt, terms of use, access policy). Prose body: anatomy of the site,
   what counts as evidence and what is ignored, pitfalls, dated log, append-only.
2. A test validates the headers (known fields, allowed values): these files must
   not accrete the way the method names did.
3. The index is generated (`make jetp-sites`): per host, number of documents,
   last result; it flags without blocking hosts with repeated failures and no
   file, and files with no active source.
4. First file: `adb.org`, from the findings of 2026-09-25 (tabs
   Overview / Project Data Sheet / Documents; agreements under
   `/projects/documents/*-lna*`, `*-ga*`, `*-grj*`; RRP `*-rrp`; sheet
   exportable as PDF, dated "Last PDS Update"; `/id/` variant in Indonesian to
   deduplicate; Cloudflare).
5. The `jetp-research` skill points to the site file before any collection at a
   host, and asks to complete it afterwards.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The collector reads the site header of each source; a source without a file follows the default profile
- [ ] Positive control: for `adb.org`, the witness document is found by the patterns; with the patterns deliberately broken, the run flags it instead of concluding "nothing new"
- [ ] A change in robots.txt or terms of use is flagged in the run report, never passed over silently
- [ ] Every distributor with at least three documents has its file
- [ ] `make check-fast` and `make lint` green
